<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēclāmātōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		declamator, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the exercise
				of speaking, declamatory, rhetorical</i> (good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de
					Or. 1, 16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illo genere duci et delectari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q.
					Fr. 3, 3 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ef.: genus dicendi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 10, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consuetudo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					5, 13, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">licentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					8, 3, 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					4, 2, 128</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">studium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 14</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēclāmātōriē</span></b> ,
				<i>in a rhetorical manner</i> (late Lat.), Hieron.
			al.</div>
